==Strategy==
Welcome to the "new" Otherworld Colosseum, which...isn't even that new considering PONOS reused a Colosseum restriction. Every unit in your lineup has the exact same cooldown (500 frames, or 16.67 seconds), meaning you're encouraged to use Super Rares for your main damage and defensive options, as well as Uber Rares which quickly become extremely unbalanced from their short cooldown.

This stage starts with two Oldhorns and a few Baa Baas, with a Boraphim after around two minutes, another Boraphim a few seconds after that, and a Hackey complicating any lure strategies you might have in mind. The best way to win is to use the starting Oldhorn to stack up anti-Angel CC units like [[Juliet the Maiko]], [[Sanzo Cat]] and [[Farmboy Cat]], while stacking sniper units to chip down Hackey like [[Jelly Dumpling Cat]]. It may be tempting to rush this stage, but at 90% base health there's another Boraphim. Only rush this stage if your units are strong enough to take down a Boraphim quickly. The Oldhorn's mostly alone, so generic anti-Relic CC like [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]] will be enough for him.

===Recommended Ubers===
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]]: Thunder Jack's fast attacks and rapid KB vs. Angel enemies allows him to be a strong unit for subduing Boraphim if you want to rush this level.
*Anti-Angel CC: Examples include [[The Peach Devils]], [[Mitama the Oracle]], and [[Fox Queen Himeyuri]].

